        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Federal test-based accountability should be judged as a math-specific achievement policy rather than a general reading reform.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "9b1f76ff9711404c861e59dc3fa7d037"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Dee and Jacob’s NCLB study reports fourth- and eighth-grade math improvement, including a 0.22 fourth-grade effect-size estimate by 2007. The same source found no evidence of fourth- or eighth-grade reading improvement, so the evidence does not support a general achievement claim.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
